    {
      "component_id": "c_032",
      "class": "com.ovuline.ovia.ui.view.TextView",
      "text": "Trying to conceive can be a new experience for lots of women, particularly those who spent years crossing their fingers and hoping NOT to get pregnant! Some women fear that their past use of birth control may permanently interfere with their chances of conceiving, but this is extremely rare. Whatever the method of birth control is, the great majority of women are able to conceive after taking birth control, even if their cycle takes some time to get back to normal.",
      "content_desc": "",
      "resource_id": "com.ovuline.fertility:id/description",
